{"id":"s4.2.2","slug":"exotic-definitions-of-numbers","title":"Exotic Definitions of Numbers","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This section introduces several unique classifications of numbers:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>Happy Number:</strong> A number whose sum of the squares of its digits eventually leads to 1. E.g., $19 \\rightarrow 1^2+9^2=82 \\rightarrow 8^2+2^2=68 \\rightarrow \\dots \\rightarrow 1$.</li><li><strong>Extravagant/Wasteful Number:</strong> A number whose prime factorization has more digits than the number itself. E.g., $18 = 2 \\times 3^2$. '18' has 2 digits, while '232' has 3.</li><li><strong>Economical/Frugal Number:</strong> The opposite of an extravagant number. E.g., $128=2^7$.</li><li><strong>Odious Number:</strong> A non-negative number with an odd number of 1s in its binary representation. E.g., $7 = 111_2$.</li><li><strong>Evil Number:</strong> A non-negative number with an even number of 1s in its binary representation. E.g., $9 = 1001_2$.</li></ul>","summary":"This section introduces several unique classifications of numbers: Happy Number: A number whose sum of the squares of its digits eventually leads to 1.","generation_guideline":"Ask for an example of a happy, extravagant, economical, odious, or evil number, or classify a given number.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Is 19 a happy number? (Yes/No)","answer":"Yes","kind":"categorical","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Is 18 an extravagant number? (Yes/No)","answer":"Yes","kind":"categorical","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Is 128 an economical number? (Yes/No)","answer":"Yes","kind":"categorical","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Is 7 an odious number? (Yes/No)","answer":"Yes","kind":"categorical","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Is 9 an evil number? (Yes/No)","answer":"Yes","kind":"categorical","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"What is the smallest happy number greater than 1?","answer":"7","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},